course: dictionary
lesson: 7564
title: Church words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word like presbyterian can look hard, but the words around it give clues. «Presbyterian churches are led by elected elders, called presbyters.» Elders are people chosen to lead, and presbyter is the name for them, so a presbyter is an elder.
explain: «Catholic, Orthodox, Anglican, Methodist and Presbyterian churches baptise babies.» This list shows that Presbyterian names one kind of church, like the others in the list. The capital P shows it is the name of a group of churches.
explain: Ask yourself: what kind of church is this? The clue «led by elected elders» tells you the members choose their leaders, not bishops. Now swap your meaning into the sentence: «Presbyterian churches are led by elders chosen by the members» still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
fact: Presbyterian is an adjective, and a Presbyterian is a noun for a member of that kind of church.
fact: «Presbyterian» describes Protestant churches that are run by elders, called presbyters.
fact: «Presbyter» means elder, a person chosen to help lead a church.
fact: The Church of Scotland is a Presbyterian church.
fact: Presbyterian churches are common in Scotland, Northern Ireland, the USA, Canada, Australia, New Zealand and Korea.
exercise: «Presbyterian churches are led by elected elders, called presbyters.» What does presbyter mean? | A type of hymn | A church building | A church bishop chosen by a king | *An elder, chosen to help lead the church
exercise: In Presbyterian churches, who chooses the elders? | The king | *The members of the church | The bishops | The Pope alone
exercise: Which country's main church is Presbyterian? | Japan | *Scotland | Egypt | Italy
test: «Presbyterian churches have roots in Scotland and in the teaching of John Calvin.» Whose teaching do Presbyterian churches have roots in? | *John Calvin | Robin Hood | Winston Churchill | Queen Victoria
test: Quakers, Pentecostals and Presbyterians are all what? | Schools | *Church families | Football clubs | Shops
exam: «Presbyterians, led by elected elders, with roots in Scotland and John Calvin» In this sentence, what does Presbyterians mean? | *People who belong to Presbyterian churches | Lutheran churches only | Quaker silence | Pentecostal worship
